  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760006,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 180 Darts: Commodore 64 - Synopsis\n\nStep up to the oche in *180 Darts*, a classic darts simulation for the Commodore 64! Test your skill and nerve in a thrilling championship tournament against a field of virtual opponents. The gameplay adheres to standard darts rules: reduce your score from 501 to zero, finishing with a precise double.\n\nBegin your ascent through the tournament, starting at the quarter-finals where you'll face opponents in best-of-three matches. Conquer the semi-finals to earn a shot at the ultimate prize – a final showdown against the formidable World Champion, \"Jammy Jim.\" Remarkably, only *one* leg is needed to defeat him and claim victory!\n\nBeyond the tournament, challenge a friend in head-to-head multiplayer or try your hand at \"Round the Clock,\" aiming to hit every number on the dartboard from 20 down to 1 within a strict time limit. *180 Darts* offers a simple yet addictive gameplay experience, perfect for honing your darts skills and proving you're the ultimate champion!"
    },
